    <summary>Reads .mbox mail archives on a Windows PC without importing them: a read-only MBOX viewer with a folder tree, header search, a date filter and single-message save or print.</summary>
    <description>This package installs an MBOX viewer for Windows that opens .mbox email archives and Thunderbird profile folders read-only, so help desk and forensic staff can browse a mailbox without importing it into any email client. The file is never modified, which keeps the copy usable as evidence or as a backup.

![MBOX Viewer Tool screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/mbv/mbv-v1-menu.png)

## How to use MBOX Viewer Tool

1. Launch the program after Chocolatey completes the install.
2. Open an .mbox file, such as a Google Takeout export or an Apple Mail MBOX file from a Mac, or choose a Thunderbird profile directory to load every mailbox in it.
3. Pick a folder in the tree and scan the list of mail.
4. Filter by Subject, From, To or a date range.
5. Click a message to read it across the full width of the window. With a license you can also save the open message from MBOX to EML, PDF or HTML.

Trial note: unregistered, the full list is visible and 3 messages a day open freely, then a countdown precedes each new one and a limit page appears after 10. A license removes the limit and enables save, print and attachments.

![MBOX Viewer Tool screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/mbv/mbv-v1-file.png)

## How to open MBOX file archives you did not create

Mail from a former employee, a client or an old company PC often arrives as a bare .mbox file. Opening it in the MBOX viewer keeps it out of your own Outlook or any other email client, and nothing goes to a server, since the program does not open a network connection. A Thunderbird profile copied from an old disk opens as the folder tree it represents.

## What the MBOX viewer shows

- The mbox file format as it is on disk: plain text mail stored back to back, split into separate letters at each From line.
- Folders Mozilla Thunderbird writes without an extension, with .msf indexes and .sbd subfolders read as part of the profile.
- Gmail exports from Google Takeout, including split parts.
- HTML formatting and inline pictures of each email.
- Long email folders that become usable while they are still loading.
- Menus and dialogs in 16 interface languages.

![MBOX Viewer Tool screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/mbv/mbv-v1-read.png)

## Who it is for

- Admins who push it with Chocolatey to help desk PCs that review mailboxes before a mail migration.
- Investigators who need an MBOX reader that leaves a mail archive unaltered on an offline machine.
- Users looking up how to open MBOX file exports on Windows who prefer a local program to an upload to someone's server.

## Trial and license

The Chocolatey package installs the free trial of a commercial program, and full use requires a license. A lifetime, 1-year, monthly or business license removes the daily reading limit and enables saving and printing. Details are on the [MBOX Viewer Tool](https://www.softorbits.net/mbox-viewer/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) page.

## FAQ

### Does Thunderbird open MBOX files?

It does after the file is imported into a profile, which copies the mailbox first. This program opens the same file directly and leaves it untouched.

### How can I get my Gmail as an MBOX file?

Export it with Google Takeout, which returns Gmail mail in .mbox format. Large exports come split into parts, and each part opens here separately.

### Can it convert an MBOX file to PDF?

It saves the email you have open as a PDF, one at a time. Converting a whole mailbox in one run is outside what this viewer does.
